{
  "message": "The good news is that the emulation found no failures: the flow is wired end to end, and no step tried to control equipment. It's still blocked, though, because none of our Google Cloud parts (Pub/Sub, Dataflow, Cloud Storage, BigQuery, Vertex AI training and Model Registry) has a native generator yet, and the two synthetic sources outside the build still need a plan for how we connect to them. A diagram change can't fix that. It needs product engineering work, and this report on artifact 2d598d4e can be used to reproduce it. I won't trim the design down to storage just to get a green result.\n\nWhile that work happens, one answer from you will shape how the generators label and test the model. How far ahead should a warning come before a likely failure, for example 7 days?",
